Machine Learning for Optimization
Standard workload: 6.0 ECTS
Learning outcomes: Students will learn fundamental concepts of solving techniques based
on machine learning and apply them to various combinatorial optimization problems.
Professional competencies: After successful completion of the module, students are able to:
• explain fundamental concepts of combinatorial optimization problems;
• explain concepts of end-to-end learning;
• explain and implement approaches based on deep learning and graph neural
networks to solve combinatorial optimization problems;
• explain and implement reinforcement learning-based approaches for combinatorial
optimization;
• apply large language models to combinatorial optimization;
